        <definition>uint32_t txn_limbo::instance_id</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>instance_id</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Instance ID of the owner of all the transactions in the queue. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Strictly speaking, nothing prevents to store not own transactions here, originated from some other instance. But still the queue may contain only transactions of the same instance. Otherwise LSN order won&apos;t make sense - different nodes have own independent LSNs in their vclock components. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
