      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structtxn__limbo_1af07ac3668341f2990e6114eb451bef08" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>struct <ref refid="structvclock" kindref="compound">vclock</ref></type>
        <definition>struct vclock txn_limbo::vclock</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>vclock</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>All components of the vclock are versions of the limbo owner&apos;s LSN, how it is visible on other nodes. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>For example, assume instance ID of the limbo is 1. Then vclock[1] here is local LSN of the instance 1. vclock[2] is how replica with ID 2 sees LSN of instance 1. vclock[3] is how replica with ID 3 sees LSN of instance 1, and so on. In that way by looking at this vclock it is always can be said up to which LSN there is a sync quorum for transactions, created on the limbo&apos;s owner node. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
